    "interlocutor_claim": [
      {
        "claim": "Harney builds on research by Denver, Ballou, and DeWitt; Harris and Socia; and Imhoff showing that stigmatizing labels worsen perceptions relative to person-first wording. Harney asks whether a label aimed at one prominent person can also harm perceptions of the wider group.",
        "quotes": [
          {
            "text": "Extant literature highlights the causal\nimpact of propagation of labels, such as ‘criminal’, to significantly worsen perceptions\nof individuals with records, relative to more humanizing, person-first language, such\nas ‘a person with a criminal record’‌‌ [8–10].",
            "page": 2
          },
          {
            "text": "The purpose of this paper was to\nidentify the potential for spillover harm that may have been caused in propagating stigmatizing labels (and/or images)\non Trump, encouraging further inquiry.",
